            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> since we don't want infix ops there (we want to use normal Lua table manipulation) (right?).\r\n\r\nyeah\r\n\r\n\r\n> Unless you mean `vim.o().listchars` would return a magic metatable; I assumed you meant it would return a normal table like `{ eol = '~', space = '-' }`.\r\n\r\nyes. but maybe metatables would be acceptable for `vim.o()` (certainly more appealing than `:append()`, etc.)\r\n\r\nbut i think infix is out of scope in any case. so i'd say we should not do this.\r\n\r\nbut thank you for the followup.",
